- Story & Context: Inside Carriage 4B on the Leipzig-Ostrava Express, shift-weary assembly worker Felix Dorn plugged a battery-powered drum box into a blown PA speaker just as the train lurched over a cracked junction. When the emergency handbrake tore loose with the stinging reek of scorched copper and cheap cherry lip gloss, the sudden screech matched the pitch of his pocket synthesizer perfectly. Instead of panicking in the dark, sixty sleepless night-shift commuters began slamming their steel-toe boots against the vibrating floorplates to a furious four-on-the-floor beat. Felix jammed a clarinet mouthpiece directly into a fuzz pedal and belted through the intercom, "Pull the cord and let the brass grease burn!"
