- Story & Context: Huddled inside the rattling baggage car near the Dresden rail siding, archivist Tova Klein felt the icy fizz of warm lemon seltzer soak into her palm as she accidentally knocked her drink into the central audio rack. Rather than cutting the power in shame, she jammed her thumb into the rewinding tape deck and confessed her deepest secret through the conductor’s horn while her soprano clarinet warbled ecstatic disco arpeggios over grinding metal riffs. The angry ticket collector dropped his ticket puncher in sheer disbelief as the insomniac passengers turned the aisle into a sweating dancefloor. Breathing hard into the feedback, Tova yelled down the corridor, "Forgive my fingers, but this railcar needs a beat!"
