Track 3: Schienenrausch at Buffer Stop Nine
- Story & Context: Legend says that by the time the night express finally rolled into Platform Nine at Warsaw Central, the brakes had completely burned down to cinder and cold morning dew coated the oxidized velvet luggage racks. Railway officials expected a riot of exhausted travelers, but instead found two hundred commuters marching off the gangway in synchronized, jolly formation with clarinets held high like torches. The locomotive’s diesel thrum had permanently retuned their nervous systems into a state of unstoppable, grinning jubilation. Before melting into the dawn crowd, the entire train car chanted in unison, "We left our sleeping pills behind the iron buffer!"
